From e7e3f2b4b1f8c14794fec3d07d1c6ef618f9f425 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Skotte <sfs@enhance-it.dk>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:39:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NetDevice: LZ4 both ways, per CPU (68020+ uploads), linked
 within a batch

An optional LZ4 encoding for Ethernet frames, used only when the board says it supports it
(LiveStatus.reserved, byte 155) and the driver says it decodes it (0x10 in
DataHeader.compressed). Board -> Amiga: LZ4 on every 68k (0xC000 | n, MFM-encoded).
Amiga -> board: LZ4 on 68020+ in place of RLE (0x4000 | n, raw); RLE on 68000/68010.
A frame's matches may reach into earlier frames of the same batch, never across batches;
LZ4 is used only when it is shorter than today's encoding. With a board that leaves byte
155 at 0 (the current Pico firmware) the driver behaves exactly as before.

webadf_lz4.c/.h and lz4_68k.asm/.h are MIT (LICENSE-lz4); LZ4.md describes the format.
